  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Missing handlers/filters in FeSL AuthZ are resulting in a bypass of authorisation (and therefore a hole in the security)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Handlers for API methods are configured in config-melcoe-pep.xml, which maps operations to the handler class for the REST and SOAP API methods.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Instead an error should be reported (and access should not be granted to the method).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Relevant code is in the REST PEP and the SOAP PEP implementations - this is where the null is tested for and the pass-through is implemented.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Sub-issues to this one identify the missing handlers/filters/mappings to handlers and filters that require implementation.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
